============================================================================================
FORBIDDEN H VALUES AS OCF/CONDORCET CYCLICITY SPECTRA
============================================================================================
H=7: formal alpha candidates up to depth 2: [(1, 1, 1), (1, 3, 0)]
       realized tournament alpha spectra in n<=6: none
H=21: formal alpha candidates up to depth 2: [(1, 0, 5), (1, 2, 4), (1, 4, 3), (1, 6, 2), (1, 8, 1), (1, 10, 0)]
       realized tournament alpha spectra in n<=6: none
Read: the social-choice object is not just 'there is a Condorcet cycle'. It is the compatible packet spectrum alpha=(1, alpha_1, alpha_2, ...). The forbidden values say certain small paradox-packet inventories cannot be simultaneously realized by any majority tournament.

============================================================================================
EXACT 3-VOTER CONDORCET SPECTRA
============================================================================================
Rows enumerate all profiles of 3 strict voters on m alternatives; unique majority tournaments are then read through the OCF spectrum.
 m   profiles  unique T  all T? H values H list
 3        216         8    True        2 [1, 3]
