Read: fixed small electorates impose extra spectra gaps, but by McGarvey the eventual electorate image is exactly the tournament image.  Thus the forbidden-H program is a statement about possible social paradox packet patterns, with voter-count refinements available as a stricter layer.

============================================================================================
IS OCF A NOISE-STABILITY FUNCTIONAL?
============================================================================================
Hard-core identity:
  mu_p(IndependentSetIndicator)=sum_I p^|I|(1-p)^(m-|I|)
  = (1-p)^m I(Omega, p/(1-p)).
  At p=2/3: H(T)=I(Omega,2)=3^m * mu_{2/3}.

Two-copy biased noise stability for rho<1 uses ordered pairs (I,J):
  Stab_{p,rho}(f)=sum_{I,J indep} P11^|I cap J| P10^|I\J| P01^|J\I| P00^outside.
  That pair spectrum is not determined by I(Omega,2) alone.

Diagonal same-state mass can be forced to activity 2 by:
  (p^2+rho*p*q)/(q^2+rho*p*q)=2, q=1-p.
     rho     p solving activity 2
       0           0.585786437627
     1/3           0.613999063671
     1/2           0.627718676731
       1           0.666666666667
Conclusion: the useful canonical statement is activity 2 / p=2/3 density. Calling it noise stability is accurate only in a degenerate rho=1 or diagonal-mass normalization; nontrivial rho asks for a richer pair polynomial.

Pair-spectrum guardrail found at n=6:
  same OCF evaluation H=23, but different pair/noise spectra
  alpha left=(1, 11, 0), alpha right=(1, 9, 1)
  tournament bits 24 and 81 have different ordered-pair spectra.
  Therefore a nontrivial noise-stability functional cannot be recovered from the OCF evaluation H alone.

